# Session end handoff

When the user says **"session end"**, **"end session"**, or **"update handoff"** (including **"session end, commit"** variants):

1. Read and follow **`~/GiT/pbx3-ops/SESSION_END_CHECKLIST.md`** (private **`aelintra/pbx3-ops`**).
2. Update:
   - `pbx3/workingdocs/TODO.md` — product roadmap only (no tip/host gossip)
   - `~/GiT/pbx3-ops/TODO_OPS.md` — tip SHAs, lab/host follow-ups
   - `~/GiT/pbx3-ops/AGENT_HANDOFF.md` — fresh **Next agent session notes** block
   - `~/GiT/pbx3-ops/SESSION_HANDOFF.md` — new top **Session end** block (skip if session was pbx3api-only with no operator impact)
3. Do not rewrite other workingdocs or `PROJECT_PLAN.md` current state.
4. Do not reintroduce session blocks into product stub handoff files.
5. Commit/push only when the user explicitly requests it in the same message (ops and product repos separately as appropriate).
6. **Optional (non-trivial code sessions):** follow the checklist’s **code-review graph** section — build/update graph in touched repos, graph-backed review before commit/push; skip docs/handoff-only sessions.

After updates, reply with a short summary of what changed in those files.
